WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.290
This is a short look at how DATOM checks the one claim a deal rests on, before the go or no go.

2
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.090
Artificial intelligence cannot be fully trusted in science.

3
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.630
Even with a search tool, it summarizes whichever papers it happens to find.

4
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.650
Asked the same question twice, it can answer differently.

5
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:31.210
That is where verification comes in: DATOM screens every paper a search returns, counts the evidence by the same rules every time, and ties each finding to the paper it came from.

6
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.460
Here is a real example from the public record.

7
00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:42.790
51 direct findings test whether GLP-1 drugs cost patients muscle as they lose weight, and 44 of them support it.

8
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.140
A simple count would put that at 86 percent.

9
00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:54.770
But many of those findings share authors and patient groups, so they are not 51 independent tests, and weighed for that the support is 68 percent.

10
00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:02.590
The verdict is still Supported, Grade A, and even the low end of the range clears the bar: act on it as supported, not as final.

11
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:12.030
A DATOM review does the same for the claim you name: a verdict, an evidence grade, and every study linked, with the ones that cut against it listed on their own.

12
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.870
It stays private and dated, and it is free of bias: only the evidence moves it.

13
00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:24.430
To start, reply to the email this came with and name your claim, or begin a review on this page.

14
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.450
DATOM.

15
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.390
Science, verified.

16
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.400
For everyone.
